{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC — hand-built from the documented response shapes in Yahoo's official",
    "Fantasy Sports API guide and from published wrapper-library samples (yfpy,",
    "yahoo_fantasy_api). NOT a live capture. Yahoo API access is gated behind an",
    "approval application and NO live call has ever been made from this repo.",
    "Replace with a real redacted capture once API access is approved, and delete",
    "this warning only when that has actually happened.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED 2026-08-11 (not captured on any date).",
    "MODELS: GET /fantasy/v2/league/461.l.576919/settings?format=json",
    "",
    "REDACTION: every identifier below is invented. League id 576919, team ids,",
    "manager GUIDs (FAKEGUID...) and the sendbird channel are all fake. No token,",
    "email, real GUID or real league key appears anywhere in this directory.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS COMMITTED: parse_league_settings() in",
    "pipelines/fantasy/providers/yahoo/parse.py fans one payload out into five",
    "tables (fantasy_league_settings, fantasy_roster_positions,",
    "fantasy_scoring_rules, fantasy_scoring_bonuses, fantasy_divisions). Nothing",
    "else in the pipeline knows how to derive starter-vs-bench slots or how to",
    "join the stat DICTIONARY to its MODIFIERS, so if this parse regresses every",
    "downstream is_starter and every reconstructed point total is wrong and",
    "nothing raises. This is the auction/divisions/keepers variant; its snake",
    "counterpart is yahoo_league_settings_snake.json.",
    "",
    "SHAPE HAZARDS DELIBERATELY PRESENT (all of them must survive parsing):",
    "  1. 'league' is a heterogeneous ARRAY: [ {metadata}, {settings: [ {...} ]} ].",
    "     Index positions shift with which sub-resources were requested — parse by",
    "     key name via flatten_resource, never by [0]/[1].",
    "  2. 'settings' is itself a one-element ARRAY, not an object.",
    "  3. Numbers are STRINGS, inconsistently: num_teams is the int 12 while",
    "     max_teams is the string \"12\", and playoff_start_week is \"15\".",
    "  4. Booleans are \"0\"/\"1\" strings.",
    "  5. max_adds is \"\" (self-closing element = 'unlimited'), NOT absent and NOT",
    "     0. faab_balance is ABSENT entirely — Yahoo documents faab_bid only as a",
    "     write input and it is unverified whether a league budget comes back on a",
    "     GET. '' vs absent vs 0 are three different claims (shape.py pathology 5).",
    "  6. roster_positions carries BN and IR+, and NEITHER has a position_type.",
    "     Starter classification therefore has to fall back to the known-name",
    "     check, which is exactly the path _parse_roster_positions guards.",
    "     is_starting_position is present on the starting slots only — also real.",
    "  7. stat_id 1 (Passing Attempts) is in stat_categories with",
    "     is_only_display_stat=1 and has NO entry in stat_modifiers: it must parse",
    "     to modifier=NULL. stat_id 3 has a modifier of literal \"0\". A stat that is",
    "     tracked but not scored is not worth zero points, and collapsing those two",
    "     is what makes 'does this league score first downs?' unanswerable.",
    "  8. Bonuses carry no id of their own; the parser mints '{stat_id}:{target}'.",
    "  9. The flex slot is labelled 'W/R/T' — its eligibility lives in the label.",
    "",
    "NOT TRUNCATED, but not exhaustive either: ~20 stat categories are included",
    "rather than Yahoo's full ~70-entry NFL dictionary, because the parser treats",
    "them uniformly and 70 near-identical entries would bury the four rows that",
    "actually exercise a distinct code path (display-only, zero-modifier, IDP-less",
    "DEF group, K distance buckets).",
    "",
    "UNVERIFIED DETAIL, stated plainly: the numeric stat_ids used here are the",
    "ones commonly published for Yahoo NFL (4=Pass Yds, 5=Pass TD, ...). They are",
    "plausible, not confirmed. Nothing in the parser depends on a particular id —",
    "only on the SAME id appearing in stat_categories and stat_modifiers — so a",
    "wrong id here cannot mask a parser bug."
  ],
